      "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{125}{(3-x)^{3}}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To simplify the expression, we write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{125}{(3-x)^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5}{(3-x)}\\cdot \\frac{5}{(3-x)}\\cdot \\frac{5}{(3-x)}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(\\frac{5}{(3-x)})}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{(3-x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
